s groaning tome. While this is indeed a viable long term hunting strategy, what it does not provide is a pragmatic reason for vampires to collaborate, only an idealistic reason. This will almost universally lead to an atomization of power and thus be ripe for steamrolling by organized groups (the Camarilla, Sabbat, Kuei Jin, etc).<br /> <br /> While the Hunter Gatherer may work well for the Gangrel, it should be noted that the Gangrel are a Clan, and not a Sect. They may identify with Anarchs, Camarilla, Sabbat, or simply disappear into the woods without reason for a century or two, simply because they want to. They are not attempting to hold territory, power or Herd, as this is a strictly &amp;quot;farming&amp;quot; mindset. A Clan is a family, and is inherent to the Blood. A Sect requires collaboration, which requires as its foundation the very thing the Anarchs attempt to undermine (Herds, and thus a cultivation of power to protect said Herd).<br /> <br /> This is an important fact to ruminate on. It all comes down to Blood and access to it. The moment you establish a Herd (night clubs, blood cults, etc), you must then defend that Herd, for your own survival. The moment you defend that Herd for your own survival, you establish a Domain. The moment you establish a Domain, you establish power bases and collaborate for mutual protection, and by that point, you've already proven your rivals correct, you're just at a different point in the continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>America\u2019s Got Talent is pretty cool sometimes \ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> But you raise some very good points and I do see being an Anarch as fundamentally a form of teen rebellion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.t