ath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T10:36:37-07:00","id":1486640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486639#post1486639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will advise you to read about the Zapatistas, who managed to hold their land against the Mexican army, or the Rojava, who have been a competent match for ISIS. Once again, you fall in the trap of confusing non hierarchical with deorganized and Hierarchal with efficient, which is a common mistake</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so explain it to me. Enlightenment me. Give me the cliff notes on these Zapatistas and Rojava.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:03:59-07:00","id":1486649,"title":"","content":"<i>Everything </i>will fail on &quot;a long enough timeline,&quot; Camarilla included. <br /> <br /> Seems to be a lot of Anarch hate here recently. Is the Carthian Movement going to have to come down here to teach the Cammies some manners? <br /> <br /> Because it's sure looking like the Carthians have to come down to the VtM board and teach some manners. /Sarcasm, I swear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:09:47-07:00","id":1486651,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs will fail of course because they'll become the Establishment.<br /> <br /> Which will create new Anarchs.<br /> <br /> In the end, vampiredom is an endless Jyhad between Neonates, Elders, freedom, and control.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T13:09:11-07:00","id":1486665,"title":"","content":"Anarchs aren't necessarily anarchs. They just aren't the Camarilla/Ashirra/Sabbat and defend a change of the status quo. A group proposing a constitution and unified leadership behind an elected figure could very well be an Anarch group. Or a great gathering of Bahari or Church of Caine zealots, lead by a religious figure. <br /> <br /> Also, a lot of these discussions seem to assume the Camarilla works as ideal, and that the Anarchs are incompetent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T13:20:49-07:00","id":1486667,"title":"","content":"'everything will fail on &quot;a long enough timeline,&quot; Camarilla included' true but the camarilla has been more successful then the anarchs who not had much successful overall and we have to ask why is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27369,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","user":"The smiling gun-knight","date":". 07-16-2022, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T13:39:39-07:00","id":1486669,"title":"","content":"'a lot of these discussions seem to assume the Camarilla works as ideal, and that the Anarchs are incompetent' well the camarilla has been around for five centuries so the camarilla way of doing things must have some merit to it, As for the anarchs I don't think most people believe they are incompetent the anarchs are very good at overthrowing the establish order but they have problems with what they will replace the old order with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T14:18:22-07:00","id":1486672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486640#post1486640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so explain it to me. Enlightenment me. Give me the cliff notes on these Zapatistas and Rojava.</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets into some serious weeds regarding how hierarchy is defined in a political organizational sense.<br /> <br /> But the basics for both groups (as they operate on similar principles) is that all authority is granted by direct democracy Anyone with the power to &quot;give orders&quot; was granted that power by the subjects of those orders, who can never lose the power to revoke that authority. So, while in battle, their armed forces have a standard military chain of command (aka there are people giving orders) it cannot be considered a true hierarchy because all of the soldiers have the power to vote out their leaders for different leaders if they don't like how the military is being run. A general is never superior to their troops, as their troops are part of the directly democratic body that sets the rules for how military commanders can legally act. The general is immediately authorized to give orders, but is ultimately socially and politically subordinate to their soldiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486649#post1486649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems to be a lot of Anarch hate here recently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's more of a case of &quot;hate&quot; for how the books treat the Anarchs, where a lot of us see potential for them as a much better setting element than they're currently being used as. Or to put it another way, we love the idea of the Anarchs, but hate the implementation given to us... hence a lot of discussions about how to better present them, or tweak them to make better use of their potential. Those threads wouldn't happen if people just hated the idea of them.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> To the OP:<br /> <br /> The problem with the whole long post is that the goals of the Anarchs are never defined, so &quot;inevitable failure&quot; is impossible to pass judgement on. Since the Anarchs do not, as a generality, advocate for the complete dismantling of having vampire societies they aren't proven wrong by creating vampire societies once they gain control over a territory.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs aren't talking about becoming your grossly oversimplified take on the Gangrel, because they're ultimately not separated from the Camarilla and Sabbat by what to do about local organizational matters. Their focus is on how strong centralized authority should be. The Camarilla has always been an organization with strong centralized authority, and the Sabbat became that before V5 nuked them as a functional organization. The Anarchs seek less centralization if not outright decentralization on an international level. The Anarchs do not believe that the Camarilla's Inner Circle, or the Sabbat's Regency are good methods for setting laws that apply to all members of their organizations, or setting policies to handle internal disputes, due to skewed priorities of such centralized power being threats to stable blood supply (as the Inner Circle and Regent are far removed from such concerns in any given city), and want a system with greater authority given to local vampires in how large scale vampire society is run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T14:18:35-07:00","id":1486673,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest issues Anarchs have with building their organization is that everyone has an idea for what they want the Anarchs to be, but are unwilling to work with others if they dont have the same idea. This doesent exactly do the movement any favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T14:46:05-07:00","id":1486675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486672#post1486672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their focus is on how strong centralized authority should be. The Camarilla has always been an organization with strong centralized authority, and the Sabbat became that before V5 nuked them as a functional organization. The Anarchs seek less centralization if not outright decentralization on an international level. The Anarchs do not believe that the Camarilla's Inner Circle, or the Sabbat's Regency are good methods for setting laws that apply to all members of their organizations, or setting policies to handle internal disputes, due to skewed priorities of such centralized power being threats to stable blood supply (as the Inner Circle and Regent are far removed from such concerns in any given city), and want a system with greater authority given to local vampires in how large scale vampire society is run.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see how the camarilla is a example of a centralized organization the inner circle doesn't have much control over the princes even the feared justicars know better then to start ordering a prince around in his or her own city nor do the inner circle interfere with the local politics of a city unless it in danger of falling to the sabbat or some other group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T14:56:27-07:00","id":1486676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486669#post1486669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well the camarilla has been around for five centuries so the camarilla way of doing things must have some merit to it,</div> </div> </div> </div>From a vampire perspective it is like a completely new form of government with just 40 years or so. Good, but far from proving anything yet when a lot of living people have first hand memories of living under another, more long lived system, and this being toppled.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnyway, my only addition to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> here is that a lot of the heat on those discussions is that a lot of people here have extremely specific views on the Anarchs that aren't necessarily the only truth, or even true at all, so end up debating the Sect standing on conflicting assumptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:16:43-07:00","id":1486683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486675#post1486675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't see how the camarilla is a example of a centralized organization the inner circle doesn't have much control over the princes even the feared justicars know better then to start ordering a prince around in his or her own city nor do the inner circle interfere with the local politics of a city unless it in danger of falling to the sabbat or some other group.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that (at least pre-V5) the Camarilla's central authority was generally wise enough to exercise their authority judiciously does not mean they do not have that authority. The V5 metaplot has them exercise quite a bit of their power to completely rework how the Camarilla operates on a local level, showing what happens when they decide to put their feet down (and negative consequences as well to that not being as effective as they like).<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> To add to monteparnas's point a bit, the Camarilla still has founding members active in the organization (even of had applies as of V5 to the Inner Circle itself). Most of the leadership is second or third &quot;generation&quot; in terms of how many people have held those seats so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-16-2022, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:38:40-07:00","id":1486689,"title":"","content":"My understanding of the backlash against anarchs is in the context of how they're emphasised as the protagonist faction with the implication the carmarilla and ashirra arnt (and the explicit with the Sabbat.) <br /> When combined their obvious status ad creators pet despite also being underwriten means they're a focal point for a lot of frustrations with v5<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is frustrating because I used to like the anarchs.<br /> <br /> Without going too far down the rabbit hole of political philosophy, for the anarch political movement to be a long lasting impact has to accommodate, circumvent or at least account for problems with vampire nature. Both the Sabbat and carmarilla establish laws and cultural trends to ensure internal stability. Anarchs don't, so for the anarch movement to actually work the game needs to implement some ideas to prevent kratocracy. It doesn't have to be Chomsky with fangs but they need something to push for rather than simply anti elder frustrations acted out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-16-2022, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:45:09-07:00","id":1486697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486689#post1486689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding of the backlash against anarchs is in the context of how they're emphasised as the protagonist faction with the implication the carmarilla and ashirra arnt (and the explicit with the Sabbat.)<br /> When combined their obvious status ad creators pet despite also being underwriten means they're a focal point for a lot of frustrations with v5</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I don't think outside of the Camarilla and Anarch books there's much focus on the Anarchs as protagonists.<br /> <br /> Jason Carl did most of the attempts to redeem the concept with the canonical LA BY NIGHT stream.<br /> <br /> WINTER'S TEETH as well. And the concept of Winter's Teeth is that the protagonist is an EX-Anarch.<br /> <br /> All of the Onyx Path supplements have had a more even handed approach to everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T17:51:53-07:00","id":1486702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486697#post1486697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly, I don't think outside of the Camarilla and Anarch books there's much focus on the Anarchs as protagonists.<br /> <br /> Jason Carl did most of the attempts to redeem the concept with the canonical LA BY NIGHT stream.<br /> <br /> WINTER'S TEETH as well. And the concept of Winter's Teeth is that the protagonist is an EX-Anarch.<br /> <br /> All of the Onyx Path supplements have had a more even handed approach to everything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've heavily alterered the settings status quo to give the anarchs a massive boost in numbers, credability and territory at the expense of the other two sects, the political aspects setting itself in v5 is framed as dissendent movements represented by anarchs and young kindred as default protagonist with carmarilla taking an implicit antagonis role. I think you're right that oynx path are less interested in the anarchs but from I've seen of design for v5 the intent is overt. With the Implosion of v5s core design group following the incident onyx path are the only surviving arm.<br /> <br /> <br /> I know you're a big fan of anarchs but you can't really argue that anarchs havnt been heavily favoured over Sabbat right?<br /> <br /> As a side i ultimatly percieve v5s anarch push as hitting simular issues as 92 on vtm had. The presence of this and other threads ultimatly reflects issues with how they're written and another potential drift away from them in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-16-2022, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T17:56:42-07:00","id":1486703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486669#post1486669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'a lot of these discussions seem to assume the Camarilla works as ideal, and that the Anarchs are incompetent' well the camarilla has been around for five centuries so the camarilla way of doing things must have some merit to it, As for the anarchs I don't think most people believe they are incompetent the anarchs are very good at overthrowing the establish order but they have problems with what they will replace the old order with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Societies, including vampiric ones, change. Governments that once work don't necessarily do it forever.<br /> The Roman Republic endured more than 500 years, and it's successor the Roman Empire almost 500 more. I think nobody would defend having then again.<br /> Likewise, the Camarilla supposed an improvement over the previous system, specially because it gave younger Kindred some measure of rights. In modern night has become a force for evil and oppression. <br /> Additionally, I think you should examine your priorities about what constitutes a good government. In my opinion, lasting longer doesn't necessarily make you better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T18:15:46-07:00","id":1486705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486703#post1486703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Likewise, the Camarilla supposed an improvement over the previous system, specially because it gave younger Kindred some measure of rights. In modern night has become a force for evil and oppression.<br /> Additionally, I think you should examine your priorities about what constitutes a good government. In my opinion, lasting longer doesn't necessarily make you better</div> </div> </div> </div>No one here is talking about which one is a good government because this is a game. While it is a commentary on politics (even if some players like the setting, but not the authors' political leanings), liking this or that in a fictional Sect or defending this or that Sect as more successful in the setting shouldn't be directly confused with one's political leanings.<br /> <br /> Take care where you're threading. VtM's Anarchs aren't real life Anarchists and shouldn't be confused with them, that isn't healthy for you. This isn't a political discussion, it is a discussion about a fictional faction being or not bound to success or failure on their fictional terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T20:13:58-07:00","id":1486711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486702#post1486702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've heavily alterered the settings status quo to give the anarchs a massive boost in numbers, credability and territory at the expense of the other two sects, the political aspects setting itself in v5 is framed as dissendent movements represented by anarchs and young kindred as default protagonist with carmarilla taking an implicit antagonis role. I think you're right that oynx path are less interested in the anarchs but from I've seen of design for v5 the intent is overt. With the Implosion of v5s core design group following the incident onyx path are the only surviving arm.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think OPP did a great job with the Anarchs in &quot;The Chicago Trilogy&quot; but obviously they aren't important in Blood Cults or its spinoffs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know you're a big fan of anarchs but you can't really argue that anarchs havnt been heavily favoured over Sabbat right?<br /> <br /> As a side i ultimatly percieve v5s anarch push as hitting simular issues as 92 on vtm had. The presence of this and other threads ultimatly reflects issues with how they're written and another potential drift away from them in setting. </div> </div> </div>I fully admit to my Anarch bias and that it blinds me to some of V5's flaws. I should point out that my SECOND favorite sect is the Sabbat and I feel like there were a lot of massive mistakes with them so if you think I'm a defender of V5 and the Sabbat, let me state otherwise. I feel V:TM is an adult game and making any group &quot;too evil&quot; to play misses the point.<br /> <br /> Still, I do think there's an argument that V5 isn't so much actually making dramatic changes to the setting as they are undoing a lot of the changes that had preexistingly shit on the Anarchs. How a lot of people feel about the Sabbat (including myself) is how I feel about how the Anarchs were treated in Revised.<br /> <br /> * Destroying the Anarch Free States so the Kuei-Jin could get some cheap heat.<br /> <br /> * Having Salvador become a collaborator with the Kuei Jin.<br /> <br /> * Making the Sabbat the primary enemy of the Camarilla vs. the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> * Dramatically increasing the Sabbat's territory in North America while getting rid of the Anarchs control over California.<br /> <br /> * Not including the Anarchs in any relavent way in the Gehenna or Thin Bloods storylines.<br /> <br /> * No Anarch Signature characters. Not a one.<br /> <br /> * The Anarchs are barely mentioned in ANY of the Revised Clan Books.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until Bloodlines any remembered they existed.<br /> <br /> V20 earned a lot of respect for me with Anarchs Unbound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T20:28:53-07:00","id":1486712,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Jenna Cross both an Anarch and a Thin Blood? I thought she had a major role in Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T20:47:43-07:00","id":1486713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486705#post1486705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one here is talking about which one is a good government because this is a game. While it is a commentary on politics (even if some players like the setting, but not the authors' political leanings), liking this or that in a fictional Sect or defending this or that Sect as more successful in the setting shouldn't be directly confused with one's political leanings.<br /> <br /> Take care where you're threading. VtM's Anarchs aren't real life Anarchists and shouldn't be confused with them, that isn't healthy for you. This isn't a political discussion, it is a discussion about a fictional faction being or not bound to success or failure on their fictional terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware that this is a discussion about a fictional setting. Curiously, though, the arguments given against are a fictional faction are exactly the same that are usually employed against RL anarchism (you can no have complex economic system or defend your community without hierarchy and why trying something new when he have a system that sucks but has endured for X years).<br /> Now, if someone were to focus on THE big problem that makes Anarchs less feasible IG than IRL (elders and inmortality) we would be having an interesting conversation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T22:34:15-07:00","id":1486717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486713#post1486713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware that this is a discussion about a fictional setting. Curiously, though, the arguments given against are a fictional faction are exactly the same that are usually employed against RL anarchism</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of that and the only reason I didn't also said those are stupid arguments as presented is because I think others already did a better job. Plus, in <b>both</b> cases, it again misses the point that the arguing person is actually arguing their own concept of the thing rather than trying to understand the thing itself.<br /> <br /> But while I understand your anger against those arguments, it doesn't change that you shouldn't take any of this as the poster defending a given system just because they thin that system is more likely to succeed. At least not until they actually and overtly say that, then it is fair play, but no one up to now said the Camarilla is the kind of government they want irl.<br /> <br /> Likewise, while I completely understand the appeal for a rl Anarchist to use the Anarchs as indeed Anarchists, and it isn't completely unintended on the authors part, in the end they're not Anarchists in the game because they're not defined under any particular political ideology. Anarchs are the rebels against the Camarilla, according to the Domain and to the particular characters doing so, and the ST or city book author decides whatever that means in their city. They <b>can</b> be Anarchists, but they can be of any political ideology as long as in context they're the rebels against the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:28:29-07:00","id":1486728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486712#post1486712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Jenna Cross both an Anarch and a Thin Blood? I thought she had a major role in Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a little pushback at the very end so it wasn't 100% shitting on the anarchs all the time but it certainly felt like it at times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:36:19-07:00","id":1486731,"title":"","content":"<b>How Mark Rein Hagen viewed the Anarchs</b><br /> <br /> I feel the need to bring up an irony of 1st Edition Anarchs that I believe is kind of interesting and relevant to this thread. I've talked with V:TM's original writer many times and read his discussions and one of the funny things about them is that he absolutely intended the Anarchs to be one of the main factions--and he also absolutely wrote them to be tools.<br /> <br /> Mark Rein Hagen envisioned the Camarilla Princes to be the &quot;enemy&quot; of the PCs but he also envisioned the system that opposed them to be equally corrupt in its own way. The working class rhetoric and &quot;fight the power&quot; of the capital A Anarchs was something he envisioned as having been co-opted by the Elders every bit as much as the more overt Camarilla.<br /> <br /> To use an example from non-vampire media in <i>The Boys</i>, Vought Media is our heroes' enemy because it controls all of the superheroes and is allied with the Right from the US government. It is opposed by an idealistic US Congresswoman who attacks Vought all the time. Our heroes initially see her as an ally against Vought and indeed give a huge amount of information to them as well as surrender many advantages. Which proves to be a mistake because it turns out she's ALSO in the employ of Vought and they attempt to control their own opposition.<br /> <br /> Mark Rein Hagen envisioned the leader of Chicago's Anarchs, Juggler, to be someone who ultimately was there to be sound and fury signifying nothing. We also find out this also applies to the High Humanity Maldavis. The Council Wars were waged by Maldavis in the Eighties and she came INCHES of overthrowing Lodin before the rug was pulled out from under her. Why? Because Maldavis was never more than a stick the Primogen of the city was using to reign in Chicago's Prince and force concessions out of him.<br /> <br /> The PCs might become free weapons against the Elders but never an NPC to follow.<br /> <br /> V:TM is fundamentally a game about PARANOIA and BETRAYAL so that you can never really &quot;win&quot; the game by allying with any particular faction because you never know who their loyalties really lie with.<br /> <br /> And this is actually why every Elder eventually is isolated and lacks the support of a coterie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2022, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:00:48-07:00","id":1486736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486636#post1486636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How? How do you guard territory or resources with no one giving orders? How do you efficiently attack weak-points in an enemy's defenses with no one giving orders? There's a saying in the military, &amp;quot;a good plan now beats a brilliant plan tomorrow&amp;quot;. That saying is all about how huge an advantage being able to give orders and have them obeyed immediately is. So much of an advantage that even a genius would be crushed by the merely competent if the merely competent can have his plan enacted with speed and power while the genius has to waste a large amount of time talking others into having a consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even a half baked plan now is better than a brilliant plan tomorrow. Tomorrow may be too late and we may all be long dead by then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:05:06-07:00","id":1486738,"title":"","content":"Revolutions invariably end up with insane power grabs that attracts the most ruthless and the worse kinds possible. One need to look no further than the French Revolution and the USSR, two revolutions to (rightfully) overthrow tyrants that ended up with psychopaths climbing to the top far worse than the previous guys. <br /> <br /> Yes, the anarchists idealism is doomed to failure, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:12:34-07:00","id":1486739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486738#post1486738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revolutions invariably end up with insane power grabs that attracts the most ruthless and the worse kinds possible. One need to look no further than the French Revolution and the USSR, two revolutions to (rightfully) overthrow tyrants that ended up with psychopaths climbing to the top far worse than the previous guys.<br /> <br /> Yes, the anarchists idealism is doomed to failure, indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, speaking as a historian, The French Revolution was the target of a carefully cultivated and longstanding vilification process by the rest of Europe designed to make it seem like it was the absolute worst thing ever in hopes of preventing any further attempts to spread its ideology beyond the ranks of France.<br /> <br /> People generally ignoring:<br /> <br /> 1. The King of France signed an agreement with the government that would have preserved his life and kept him as a figurehead monarch, only to immediately plan to invade his own nation with the forces of his wife to crush the revolutionaries. Which is why he was executed for treason. Because, you know, he committed treason and broke his word on what would have previously been a moderate action.<br /> <br /> 2. The Revolutionaries were anti-slavery and it was Napoleon who reinstituted that evil institution.<br /> <br /> 3. The Reign of Terror is something that pretty much everyone acts as the beginning, middle, and end of the Revolution. Its horrible events are roughly equivalent to a lot of the &quot;normal&quot; chaos of the countries around it during their turmoil but much less famous.<br /> <br /> 4. The reforms of the Revolution are what propelled Napoleon's France (which he always maintained he was defending) from a nation on the verge of collapse into a period superpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:59:00-07:00","id":1486743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486711#post1486711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, I think OPP did a great job with the Anarchs in &quot;The Chicago Trilogy&quot; but obviously they aren't important in Blood Cults or its spinoffs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I fully admit to my Anarch bias and that it blinds me to some of V5's flaws. I should point out that my SECOND favorite sect is the Sabbat and I feel like there were a lot of massive mistakes with them so if you think I'm a defender of V5 and the Sabbat, let me state otherwise. I feel V:TM is an adult game and making any group &quot;too evil&quot; to play misses the point.<br /> <br /> Still, I do think there's an argument that V5 isn't so much actually making dramatic changes to the setting as they are undoing a lot of the changes that had preexistingly shit on the Anarchs. How a lot of people feel about the Sabbat (including myself) is how I feel about how the Anarchs were treated in Revised.<br /> <br /> * Destroying the Anarch Free States so the Kuei-Jin could get some cheap heat.<br /> <br /> * Having Salvador become a collaborator with the Kuei Jin.<br /> <br /> * Making the Sabbat the primary enemy of the Camarilla vs. the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> * Dramatically increasing the Sabbat's territory in North America while getting rid of the Anarchs control over California.<br /> <br /> * Not including the Anarchs in any relavent way in the Gehenna or Thin Bloods storylines.<br /> <br /> * No Anarch Signature characters. Not a one.<br /> <br /> * The Anarchs are barely mentioned in ANY of the Revised Clan Books.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until Bloodlines any remembered they existed.<br /> <br /> V20 earned a lot of respect for me with Anarchs Unbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Cults is kinda sect neutral as more of a spinoff. Outside of heceta I'm not entirely convinced it even matters on the larger scale aka states of grace in Revised.<br /> <br /> You are partially correct about revised anarchs being downplayed but overstate your case. They had sections dedicated to them in carmarilla and their own book as a playable option. Compare to how badly v5 sabbat players have been treated <br /> <br /> Your arguement works on the assumption that the 2/revised drift away from anarchs wasn't an organic occurance in reaction to how the game developed but some sort of imposed vision. As I've mentioned before the anarchs as written in 91 or v5 arnt very good protagonist over a extended timeline. They work very well in a medium like video games where the limited narrative and play time works in their favour as a protagonist faction. But as a large scale dissedent sect they just don't work very well as written in a table top rpg. We're already seeing this problem emerging in threads on this very forum including this one. V5's biggest lore gaffe was that they unable or unwilling to do anything with the anarchs resurgence and were caught at a point where their entire reason for existence is the other sects shat the bed. <br /> <br /> So while someone who likes anarchs might grumble that revised emphasised Sabbat vs carmarilla the truth is Sabbat vs carmarilla is a FAR more compelling dynamic because the anarchs don't have enough going on to carry an large scale decades long rpg conflict in that context.<br /> <br /> Going forward the writters are going to have to shit or get off the pot. With stable domains and praxis, if they fall back on bikers and malcontents angrily calling the prince a fascist because he barely tolerates a barony you're going to see a drift in players away from the sect as a player choice again. Which I'll admit is fine by me since I prefer the other two sects by a mile and even the ashirra seem more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-17-2022, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T02:09:40-07:00","id":1486744,"title":"","content":"So on top with Anarch and Camarilla vampires:<br /> <br /> In the long run in Vampire, the oldest vampires with high level of Dominate and Presence and other such Disciplines will inevitably end up in charge. It's not much different from the United States, in that very wealthy people inevitably end up in charge. There may be a few exceptions here or there, but in the same way that people with wealth end up in charge politically, among vampires, elder vampires with certain Disciplines inevitably end up in charge.<br /> <br /> Anarchs can't really change that and any system they introduce will end up with the upper echelons being dominated by the oldest and most powerful vampires. At most they can dilute power or spread it around to keep it from being concentrated in a single individual like with Princes. But that <i>can</i> work. For example, in many Anarch territories in the Free States, they have a council of Barons. Each Baron has power over a certain era, like a part of a city, and then they work with other Barons to exert power overt the whole city. So you might have 3-7 Barons controlling a city which, if it were in the Camarilla, would see that city entirely controlled by a single Prince. Basically the vampires which, in a Camarilla city, would end up as the Primogen and working under the Prince, end up as fellow Barons in Anarch territory.<br /> <br /> That system seems like it could function, in the long term, as well as the Camarilla's system. But inevitably the same sort of vampires who would end up as Princes in the Camarilla would still end up as Barons in Anarch territory, it's just that they would have to share power with the kinds of vampires who would end up as Primogen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T02:29:45-07:00","id":1486745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486717#post1486717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Likewise, while I completely understand the appeal for a rl Anarchist to use the Anarchs as indeed Anarchists, and it isn't completely unintended on the authors part, in the end they're not Anarchists in the game because they're not defined under any particular political ideology. Anarchs are the rebels against the Camarilla, according to the Domain and to the particular characters doing so, and the ST or city book author decides whatever that means in their city. They <b>can</b> be Anarchists, but they can be of any political ideology as long as in context they're the rebels against the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah I've noticed that v5 leans hard into suggesting them as anarchists in terms of presentation even though they're not. I think the back blurb of v5 said something like &quot;anarchs are to anarchy as monarchs are to monarchy.&quot; Or somesuch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T02:48:00-07:00","id":1486746,"title":"","content":"To be fair, there are many anarchists in the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> There are also outright fascists.<br /> <br /> Which is why the Anarchs are as effective as the Judean People's Front but not the People's Front of Judea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:01:46-07:00","id":1486767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486739#post1486739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, speaking as a historian, The French Revolution was the target of a carefully cultivated and longstanding vilification process by the rest of Europe designed to make it seem like it was the absolute worst thing ever in hopes of preventing any further attempts to spread its ideology beyond the ranks of France.<br /> <br /> People generally ignoring:<br /> <br /> 1. The King of France signed an agreement with the government that would have preserved his life and kept him as a figurehead monarch, only to immediately plan to invade his own nation with the forces of his wife to crush the revolutionaries. Which is why he was executed for treason. Because, you know, he committed treason and broke his word on what would have previously been a moderate action.<br /> <br /> 2. The Revolutionaries were anti-slavery and it was Napoleon who reinstituted that evil institution.<br /> <br /> 3. The Reign of Terror is something that pretty much everyone acts as the beginning, middle, and end of the Revolution. Its horrible events are roughly equivalent to a lot of the &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; chaos of the countries around it during their turmoil but much less famous.<br /> <br /> 4. The reforms of the Revolution are what propelled Napoleon's France (which he always maintained he was defending) from a nation on the verge of collapse into a period superpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didnt try to say that the French Revolution wasnt deserved - or even necessary. In both cases the autocrats and rulling classes of both French and Russia were total dicks.<br /> <br /> My point was simply that the end result of said revolutions is horrendous tragedy. But both were both inevitable and perhaps even necessary (given the circumstances)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:11:59-07:00","id":1486768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486746#post1486746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, there are many anarchists in the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> There are also outright fascists.<br /> <br /> Which is why the Anarchs are as effective as the Judean People's Front but not the People's Front of Judea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of, the People's Front of Judea, they are the absolute worse. No no no, we are the judean people's front. The Front of judean people is that guy over there. Traitor!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:48:03-07:00","id":1486787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486743#post1486743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood Cults is kinda sect neutral as more of a spinoff. Outside of heceta I'm not entirely convinced it even matters on the larger scale aka states of grace in Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is in a weird position where the majority of tabletop content produced for it is by OPP because the schedule for release has been so incredibly lackluster. OPP is also the group that cares about continuity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are partially correct about revised anarchs being downplayed but overstate your case. They had sections dedicated to them in carmarilla and their own book as a playable option. Compare to how badly v5 sabbat players have been treated </div> </div> </div>It's not a competition for being crapped upon. I also don't disagree with the Sabbat being horribly treated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your arguement works on the assumption that the 2/revised drift away from anarchs wasn't an organic occurance in reaction to how the game developed but some sort of imposed vision. As I've mentioned before the anarchs as written in 91 or v5 arnt very good protagonist over a extended timeline. They work very well in a medium like video games where the limited narrative and play time works in their favour as a protagonist faction. But as a large scale dissedent sect they just don't work very well as written in a table top rpg. We're already seeing this problem emerging in threads on this very forum including this one. V5's biggest lore gaffe was that they unable or unwilling to do anything with the anarchs resurgence and were caught at a point where their entire reason for existence is the other sects shat the bed. </div> </div> </div>I would strongly disagree with this as the Anarch resurgance has been handled pretty well in the side content like the video games, web shows, and visual novels. Ironically, the biggest endorsement is that they don't seem to have changed much from Bloodlines. They're in the same cities as the Camarilla and butting heads over turf and power but the political games move on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So while someone who likes anarchs might grumble that revised emphasised Sabbat vs carmarilla the truth is Sabbat vs carmarilla is a FAR more compelling dynamic because the anarchs don't have enough going on to carry an large scale decades long rpg conflict in that context. </div> </div> </div>That's a matter of perspective because the Sabbat can't interact with the Camarilla save at the point of a sword while Anarchs and Camarilla can't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Going forward the writters are going to have to shit or get off the pot. With stable domains and praxis, if they fall back on bikers and malcontents angrily calling the prince a fascist because he barely tolerates a barony you're going to see a drift in players away from the sect as a player choice again. Which I'll admit is fine by me since I prefer the other two sects by a mile and even the ashirra seem more interesting. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I feel like the person who is the best ambassador for the Anarchs is Jason Carl right now. He's the guy selling the Anarchs to the most people. We'll also see how the video games treat them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T12:02:17-07:00","id":1486789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486787#post1486787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a matter of perspective because the Sabbat can't interact with the Camarilla save at the point of a sword while Anarchs and Camarilla can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but not the point.<br /> <br /> It was an organic shift not because the Anarchs <b>can't</b> be better used, but because they just hadn't been. By the time <i>Revised</i> came with the stated goal of laying the bed for the end of the world, it was too late to lift the Anarchs and then use them.<br /> <br /> And this is the problem. The Anarchs were the protagonists in 1st ed, arguably the protagonists in 2nd ed and certainly the protagonists in 5th ed. But they're still being badly worked upon on the premise that their core trope is enough to carry them on. In the past the problem was 2nd ed authors not giving them anything interesting until it was too late, now it seems to be 5th edition authors divided between thinking not moving their <i>status quo </i>is enough and still not being all that interested on them (OPP, in a sense).<br /> <br /> My opinion is that they absolutely work as protagonists, but they also do need some competent writing to keep it up. That didn't came yet. They still have time, but it is running out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T15:08:23-07:00","id":1486801,"title":"","content":"Yes that's exactly my point, its not that the anarchs can't be an interesting group for play its that historically they arnt and if current trends continue we will hit the late 2nd/revised shift were the writting moves away from anarchs vs carmarilla or the lack of depth will begin to damage the settings viability.<br /> <br /> I mean Phipps reply kind of hints at the issue as his positive examples arnt actually the core game but spin of materials where their issues arnt apparent due to the smaller frame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-17-2022, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T18:31:49-07:00","id":1486818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486801#post1486801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes that's exactly my point, its not that the anarchs can't be an interesting group for play its that historically they arnt and if current trends continue we will hit the late 2nd/revised shift were the writting moves away from anarchs vs carmarilla or the lack of depth will begin to damage the settings viability.<br /> <br /> I mean Phipps reply kind of hints at the issue as his positive examples arnt actually the core game but spin of materials where their issues arnt apparent due to the smaller frame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly, I think a major issue is the Anarchs were never personalized.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are notable for the fact they don't have any Signature characters (except Ramona and everyone basically considers her a mistake versus Beckett). So given Revised heavily focused on the Signature characters with their novels and world travels as well as larger-than-life personalities, I feel that severely cut into the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs never really had personalities that defined so much of Revised. I feel like people underestimate just how much an important NPC can define media. Which is part of the reason why I feel like the Anarchs started regaining their cachet after Bloodlines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T21:18:47-07:00","id":1486838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486818#post1486818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is part of the reason why I feel like the Anarchs started regaining their cachet after Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines was the best thing to ever happen to the Anarchs, as it did it all: gave us nice, interesting Anarch characters, run a game into an actual Anarch Domain with actual Anarch politics that wasn't just completely generic, while giving us a good shot on what the typical Anarch is like versus the big guys (in the form of the Neonates at the bar), all the while keeping the pace of the story and the game and having them interact with things actually happening and the plot moving forward.<br /> <br /> The problem is, it was just one game. A very good one, but still only one, with very limited boundaries to work with. It can't be everything we have on them and call it a return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T21:57:24-07:00","id":1486840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486838#post1486838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines was the best thing to ever happen to the Anarchs, as it did it all: gave us nice, interesting Anarch characters, run a game into an actual Anarch Domain with actual Anarch politics that wasn't just completely generic, while giving us a good shot on what the typical Anarch is like versus the big guys (in the form of the Neonates at the bar), all the while keeping the pace of the story and the game and having them interact with things actually happening and the plot moving forward.<br /> <br /> The problem is, it was just one game. A very good one, but still only one, with very limited boundaries to work with. It can't be everything we have on them and call it a return.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the largest issues I feel with V5 is the fact that V5 feels like it wants to make everything Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T00:15:06-07:00","id":1486850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486667#post1486667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and we have to ask why is that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to be negative but it's because that's the way they were written.<br /> <br /> I feel like people have forgotten that all the various vampire sects/clans/tribes/etc are fictional and that none of them face any actual evolutionary or societal pressure to make them change, only popularity amongst the fandom. It's all too easy, given the amount of lore, to fall into the trap of actualising(?) the fiction.<br /> <br /> One of the banes of speculative fiction is building a realistic 'world' that appears, to the reader, to be consistent and whole, while being made up of only a few words and hints, and the more words that are created towards building the world the more likely that there will be contradictions and unrealistic constructions within those words.<br /> <br /> As such some of the aspects of the camarilla et al are going to be unrealistic and are there for the purpose of providing an entertaining game experience rather than a realistic socio-political simulation. Those unrealistic elements can be discussed and possibly justified but ultimately they cannot change because the books are written and published and cannot be recalled and replaced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T00:41:41-07:00","id":1486851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486850#post1486850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As such some of the aspects of the camarilla et al are going to be unrealistic and are there for the purpose of providing an entertaining game experience rather than a realistic socio-political simulation. Those unrealistic elements can be discussed and possibly justified but ultimately they cannot change because the books are written and published and cannot be recalled and replaced.</div> </div> </div> </div> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cIt's no wonder that truth is stranger than fiction. Fiction has to make sense.\u201d \u2015 Mark Twain </span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> The moment I fell in love with the World of Darkness was not V:TM but Changeling: The Dreaming and that it was when I read about the Accordance War. The Accordance War being the fight between the sidhe and their supporters invading from the moon (long story) versus the Changelings who'd grown up in a democracy.<br /> <br /> The feudalist sidhe won.<br /> <br /> I always liked that moment because it was a matter of settled law (how ironic that statement is these days) that the people who were in favor of authoritarian tyranny had triumphed and everyone had to just basically get used to it. It established a fact about the world that there was no bend towards justice and even the public could completely give up on trying to change things.<br /> <br /> It actually made the world feel much more real when I pursuing my Masters in history (before I switched to Literature).<br /> <br /> History is often full of things that make absolutely no goddamned sense given the way things SHOULD work and we often are left to rationalize them after the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T01:47:36-07:00","id":1486854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486818#post1486818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weirdly, I think a major issue is the Anarchs were never personalized.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are notable for the fact they don't have any Signature characters (except Ramona and everyone basically considers her a mistake versus Beckett). So given Revised heavily focused on the Signature characters with their novels and world travels as well as larger-than-life personalities, I feel that severely cut into the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs never really had personalities that defined so much of Revised. I feel like people underestimate just how much an important NPC can define media. Which is part of the reason why I feel like the Anarchs started regaining their cachet after Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which subtley feeds into my observation about video games of vtm verses the core game. Anarchs are written work fine as a video game faction. While the npcs are memorable the game itself doesn't really do anything different from the core book but it gets away with the lack of depth because overall you're talking about 22 hours of game length and has a far more limited range of agency than a tabletop game.<br /> <br /> You can't model an pan national faction as presented in v5 around 5-8 npcs and the stupid arsehole prince they hate. That's how you end up with the game moving towards Sabbat and carmarilla play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-18-2022, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T02:04:03-07:00","id":1486855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486854#post1486854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which subtley feeds into my observation about video games of vtm verses the core game. Anarchs are written work fine as a video game faction. While the npcs are memorable the game itself doesn't really do anything different from the core book but it gets away with the lack of depth because overall you're talking about 22 hours of game length and has a far more limited range of agency than a tabletop game.<br /> <br /> You can't model an pan national faction as presented in v5 around 5-8 npcs and the stupid arsehole prince they hate. That's how you end up with the game moving towards Sabbat and carmarilla play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is weird because the Anarchs were ORIGINALLY a pan-national fashion. The Anarch Cookbook says they're a coordinated guerilla resistance movement across the United States and presumably many other countries. Salvador Garcia wasn't just hanging around in California, he was working against every Prince everywhere.<br /> <br /> This was basically just forgotten and the Sabbat became the guys who did revolutions.<br /> <br /> The reason why?<br /> <br /> I believe it's because the WW wanted to get the Anarchs and Camarilla fighting TOGETHER against the Sabbat to unite the player base.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T02:12:29-07:00","id":1486856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486855#post1486855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is weird because the Anarchs were ORIGINALLY a pan-national fashion. The Anarch Cookbook says they're a coordinated guerilla resistance movement across the United States and presumably many other countries. Salvador Garcia wasn't just hanging around in California, he was working against every Prince everywhere.<br /> <br /> This was basically just forgotten and the Sabbat became the guys who did revolutions.<br /> <br /> The reason why?<br /> <br /> I believe it's because the WW wanted to get the Anarchs and Camarilla fighting TOGETHER against the Sabbat to unite the player base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they're not very interesting and anarch cook book like v5 anarch isn't a very good book and they needed to be a very good book. Like Sabbat revised or technocracy revised good.<br /> <br /> I think you're wrong as their isn't any evidence of this, I think more likely the Sabbat and carmarilla were simply better written 2nd ed on so the game drifted away. V5 had the opternity to change (and deliberately gutted the Sabbat and discredited the carmarilla in prep) this but has completly failed to do so, so now where hovering at 91, which is going to be a real problem moving forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-18-2022, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T05:03:50-07:00","id":1486866,"title":"","content":"I think there's a data point worth considering here: LARPs.<br /> <br /> While it's hard to speak to any specifics (I can't find any records of this left over from the mid-90s), the large fan VtM LARP organizations all drifted towards Cam vs. Sabbat before the books did. The problem was that Cam vs. Anarchs didn't work for the LARP format. This was a big place where the &quot;Camarilla-lite&quot; attitude snuck in. Anarchs as-written weren't good for LARPs (and personalization wasn't the problem). LARPs work better with the Cam as the PCs (organization multiple local events under one larger organization is much much much easier to do with the Cam than the Anarchs), and the Sabbat work better as the antagonists to Cam LARPs (as the Sabbat has a lot more too offer than just a bunch of angry young vampires with a smart leader).<br /> <br /> The TTRPG books followed the trend far more than the other way around. LARPs were more Cam focused. The big event LARPs at conventions and so on followed suit. The visibility of defaulting to Cam PCs grew, and the more able Sabbat antagonists grew with it. <br /> <br /> It's far more likely the oWW was following the players' lead more than the other way around here. The supplement treadmill needs people to buy buy buy, and you need to sell to what they're playing more than you get to direct popularity via editorial decisions (the oWW walked back a lot of 2e and Rev. metaplot stuff because it was unpopular and thus wasn't selling as well)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:04:13-07:00","id":1486870,"title":"","content":"Ultimately, the lore of WoD is not realistic in an overall global sense; it can be used as is for local stories, but the moment you try to apply it on a global sense, it makes no sense.<br /> <br /> What I mean by that: I did once tried to &quot;run a simulation&quot; of all the different groups - a simple &quot;division of labor&quot; of the massive multitude of groups, based on the &quot;official&quot; numbers of supernaturals that supposedly inhabit the world.<br /> <br /> Just you guys try to do that, and you'll perceive how that doesnt lend itself to the stories being told. For example, the number of Cainites in the world is suppose to be at 40.000<br /> <br /> Now, try to divide that in at least 15 - 13 clans, plus a number of bloodlines and caithffs. Lets round those 40k to 60k for the math, and also because that number was from the 90's. That gives roughly 4.000 vampires to each clan - now now, I know they dont all have the exact same numbers, but that just adds injury to the insult. And, we'd get also 8000 ones to divide among the numerous bloodlines, caithffs and possibly antitribu.<br /> <br /> Ok, now divide that among the specific inter clans political/philosophical divisions.<br /> <br /> Now, try to divide that between generations, while quickly realizing that generational numbers add up upon one another exponentionally. So, aside from the 13 third generations, we are left with 9 generations to divide that - and there are also thin bloods. So, that gives almost 400 of each generation for each clan, which wouldnt be as such due to the exponential progression of it, but it does give an idea.<br /> <br /> Now, for vampires that is still somewhat viable, althought unlikely given the stories told. But the case gets far worse for the other splats.<br /> <br /> The worse offender by far is Mage. Mages &quot;official&quot; number is 1 in a million. If we are generous, that gives the impressive number of 8.000 mages globally.<br /> <br /> Now, between Mages we have basically 5 major &quot;factions&quot;: the Technocracy, Traditions, Disparates, Nefandi and Marauders.<br /> <br /> Let's be ultra generous and round them to 9.000 and divide by 3, with the Disparates taking one of the portions along with Nefandi and Marauders, since those are obviously smaller. And lets wave the fact that probably the Technocracy have far more enlightned people than the Traditions, but lets just equalize the numbers. That gives 3.000 mages for each faction.<br /> <br /> Ok, now let us divide those 3.000 Mages between the Traditions, for instance. That will gives a number of 300-350 Mages in each Tradition, and only if we are been ULTRA generous.<br /> <br /> Now, divide those 300 mages in each tradition between the several houses of the Order of Hermes, and you'll realize that the might and powerful hermetic houses are actually a rabble of a few dozens of secluded weirdos in a very very localized ponctual way.<br /> <br /> Now, let us think about how many of those are truly on Earth. Because you know, there are several places in Umbra to stay, Horizon, Doissetep, the Digital Web... And all of a sudden, the &quot;house Flambeau&quot; constantly &quot;waging war&quot; against the Union becomes just a pathetically small gang fight of that one single guy that was left on the material plane.<br /> <br /> And if you try to think how many masters there are for each group, it gets even worse! It's no more than half a dozen for each.<br /> <br /> Not enough for be building an armada fleet of starships, or armies of clones.<br /> <br /> So, all the lore must be considered locally for making enjoyable stories, but is not realistic in a global sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T10:17:03-07:00","id":1486884,"title":"","content":"That reminds me of something I've noticed from movies: no matter how large or small the setting of a war movie is, it always seems to involve the same number of characters and even visible extras. Star Wars is a huge setting, with a huge chunk of the galaxy inhabited with hundreds of billions, perhaps trillions, of people and contributing soldiers. Movies like &quot;300&quot; and &quot;Troy&quot; are about tiny city-states fighting other tiny city-states. Yet somehow the visible number of main characters and extras are roughly the same. That's because these movies are about drama, and the number of characters in a war drama doesn't vary much regardless of the official populations involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T14:23:24-07:00","id":1486908,"title":"","content":"There's also limits to what's practical in any given medium. The number of &quot;main&quot; characters on-screen and in-script have some pretty well trod estimates of how many you can have before you start losing the audience in a film; whereas books tend to be able to have much larger leading casts as there isn't the expectation of being able to digest the whole story in a few hours. Older films tend to have way less extras than new films because of changes in technology. Movies like the LotR series and 300 use digital technology to turn a few hundred extras into thousands of individuals on screen: something older war films couldn't do and used other methods to imply the massive size of groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T15:11:11-07:00","id":1486917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486870#post1486870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, the lore of WoD is not realistic in an overall global sense; it can be used as is for local stories, but the moment you try to apply it on a global sense, it makes no sense.<br /> <br /> What I mean by that: I did once tried to &quot;run a simulation&quot; of all the different groups - a simple &quot;division of labor&quot; of the massive multitude of groups, based on the &quot;official&quot; numbers of supernaturals that supposedly inhabit the world.<br /> <br /> Just you guys try to do that, and you'll perceive how that doesnt lend itself to the stories being told. For example, the number of Cainites in the world is suppose to be at 40.000</div> </div> </div> </div>It is?<br /> <br /> I thought the number of vampires was supposed to be 1 for every 100,000 people in the world and that was also the &quot;ideal&quot; number rather than how many actual vampires there were in the world. With the implication the number of undead in the world was also grossly overpopulated.<br /> <br /> I think at my table, I said all of the 13 Clans had about 2000 members each, the Bloodlines had a few hundred, and the Caitiff and Thin Bloods each had their own Clan numbers now.<br /> <br /> I think I also established that this was for Europe, North America, and South America too, which meant no one had any idea how many vampires were in Asia or Africa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The worse offender by far is Mage. Mages &quot;official&quot; number is 1 in a million. If we are generous, that gives the impressive number of 8.000 mages globally. </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is ridiculous. It's also doubly weird because mages can exist outside of reality in Horizon Realms by the thousands and mages are far-far more easier to live among us than the undead. Indeed, there's a lot more support for people who believe they're magic-users in RL even without including super-scientists.<br /> <br /> One of my STs tried to compensate by suggesting 9 out of 10 Mages were actually Hedge Mages and the 1 in a million was a True Magic user. Which is something that has no support.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for doing the math.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T19:04:39-07:00","id":1486931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486840#post1486840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the largest issues I feel with V5 is the fact that V5 feels like it wants to make everything Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe this phrase actually encapsulates V5 better than saying it tries to be 1st edition. For the good and the bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486866#post1486866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a data point worth considering here: LARPs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point.<br /> <br /> In the end, LARPs work mostly for the social/political play, while the Anarchs were built for the kind of story where you have a small band of protagonists. It was built for TT PCs, where you're either the small band working through the mysteries and conspiracies to be the heroes of the revolution, or the task force working to weed out the dangerous rebels without destabilizing the city. There are very few ways to make such a story engage dozens of players at once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486917#post1486917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my STs tried to compensate by suggesting 9 out of 10 Mages were actually Hedge Mages and the 1 in a million was a True Magic user. Which is something that has no support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure it has no support? I've always thought that the 1 in a million figure was exactly about the Awakened and not any Magic-User.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:04:45-07:00","id":1486937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486931#post1486931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure it has no support? I've always thought that the 1 in a million figure was exactly about the Awakened and not any Magic-User.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, the 1 in a million is the number of Awakened Mages, not hedge magicians (or exceptional citizens). That's still... Meh. The cool stuff - Autochtonia, Mecha, Doissetep - those things cannot be built by hedge magicians, and hedge magic sucks anyway, both in terms of mechanics and in terms of a concept or lore.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the same goes for all the other splats; I did the math for all of them using every possible official source I could get, and you'd have things like 18 k Garou, 12 k of the other Fera and 12 k Changellings, and once you start the divisions between all the breeds, tribes and then to aggravate it all, the writters always have the impetus of adding more and more and more and you end up with all the internal subdivisions... I guess you can all get the picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:36:01-07:00","id":1486941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486931#post1486931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure it has no support? I've always thought that the 1 in a million figure was exactly about the Awakened and not any Magic-User.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but it also doesn't really change the presentation either.<br /> <br /> None of the lore presented in Mage: The Ascension presents the Awakened as being an elite of the Traditions but how your average apprentice, Disciple, and Master goes. It'd be different if there were hundreds of Order of Hermes sorcerers for every truly magnificent will-worker like pianists to Mozart but we don't get that. Frankly, I kind of wish that was the way things were because it would recontextualize things a bit more. SOME magical gods exist who can define reality and most are just guys recruited and trained in the Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Ironically, the only organization for support like this is the Technocracy that IS portrayed as utterly massive and there's a constant emphasis on how they have tens of thousands of employees and thousands of people who can do SOME of their magic. However, there's no rules support for their Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:37:22-07:00","id":1486943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486917#post1486917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is?<br /> <br /> I thought the number of vampires was supposed to be 1 for every 100,000 people in the world and that was also the &amp;quot;ideal&amp;quot; number rather than how many actual vampires there were in the world. With the implication the number of undead in the world was also grossly overpopulated.<br /> <br /> I think at my table, I said all of the 13 Clans had about 2000 members each, the Bloodlines had a few hundred, and the Caitiff and Thin Bloods each had their own Clan numbers now.<br /> <br /> I think I also established that this was for Europe, North America, and South America too, which meant no one had any idea how many vampires were in Asia or Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>The number of 40 k cainites was for the 90's, when there was getting close to 7 billion people (but not there yet), so that consideration runned the idea of having 30 k Kuei Jin. Yeah, all that using the conservative estimates of 100 k humans per vampire.<br /> <br /> But that is now, and that is now that we have massive sprawling cities of millions of people.<br /> <br /> Take Dark Ages however, when the human population was estimated to be about 200 millions. We've only had 1 billion people for around the 19th century. For 200 millions, that would give the impressive amount of... Wait for it - 2.000 vampires. To divide among 13 clans, antitribu, bloodlines, caitiff, internal clan divisions... And that if we dont consider the Kuei Jin at all.<br /> <br /> Also, the major european cities had less than 100 thousand people. The only cities before the 19th century that had over 1 million people were Rome and Tenochtitlan (Mexico City nowadays, the former capital of the aztecs). This would hold true until London reached the number of 1 million in the 19th century!<br /> <br /> So, just imagine those 2.000 vampires living over a few dozens of cities with usually around 10 thousand people at most. And now you'll just begin to understand the problem.<br /> <br /> I wont even go into the absolutely ridicule idea that the &quot;war&quot; of Ascension between the Traditions and Order of Reason would have to be ignited by a few gangs of weirdos whose total ranks about 200 individuals - if you ever counter every single freaking mage drawing breath in the entire world.<br /> <br /> So, the house of Tremere probably was comprised ONLY OF TREMERE! Hahahaha. There was the archmage Tremere in it and... Yep. This is it. The entire house. Lol.<br /> <br /> This also means that you have 2000 vampires to not only divide among tons of different vampiric families - and subcultures within these families - but also those 2000 to divide between the earlier generations, which in DA could go up to 12th generation at char gen. And that at least 95% of all cainites in the world have less than a century.<br /> <br /> Also, most &quot;princes&quot; in DA were only &quot;princes&quot; of something because they were the only vampire in the entire city.<br /> <br /> It's absolutely nonsensical.<br /> <br /> On the other hand thou, at the same time that those numbers are too small, they are also too big.<br /> <br /> I'll explain, and it's fairly simple: &quot;human helpers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Vampires have ghouls. How many? Hard to tell since there's no official sources, but between normal ghouls, tzimisce and tremere revenants and the need for pawns for protection, it's not unreseanable to assume anywhere between 1 to 10 ghouls/revenants per vampire. If we want to remain conservative, we can go with 1. That's another 40 k ghouls - or straight up 80k ghouls, disregarding Kuei Jins, and that could go as far as 800.000<br /> <br /> Then comes Mages. &quot;Extraordinary citizens&quot; are almost everywhere for the Union, so much so that I wouldnt blink an eye if it were on the proportion of 1 to 100. So again, that could go from another 8000 to 800.000 or more of human mortals who are part of the &quot;shadow conspiracy&quot; of the supernaturals; if you feel that's too much, I would still insist this number is no less than 80k and probably much more.<br /> <br /> And you do the same exercise for the Fera kin, and you'll get what I mean.<br /> <br /> This means that the &quot;sleepers&quot;, all of a sudden are much less common. Yes, still billions of them. But between Fomoris, ghouls, acolites and even hunters! there's little very little room for the common man to be anything but peasants; the moment you stick your head above the average masses you're recruited by some crazy supernatural shit to serve as low rank in some weird hidden war.<br /> <br /> That also means that ALL &quot;humans&quot; of note must have some supernatural &quot;patron&quot;. And when the books talk about human agency and how &quot;humans need not supernaturals to commit atrocities&quot;, that a big lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:41:25-07:00","id":1486946,"title":"","content":"All very good points, thank you.<br /> <br /> I think V: TDA actually went with Europe being incredibly grossly overpopulated with vampires so it was more like &quot;one vampire per ten thousand people.&quot; Which, of course, was meant to set up the Inquisition and also the fact the Dark Ages were meant to be a somewhat Hollywoodized version of themselves which was closer to Castlevania than actual historical accuracy. I admit I liked that part of Transylvania By Night.<br /> <br /> &quot;Disclaimer - There weren't elaborate Hapsburg-esque massive castles in Romania at this time or, in fact, ever but there are here because Tzimisce, Tremere, and Ventrue. Deal.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:03:07-07:00","id":1486990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486937#post1486937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right, the 1 in a million is the number of Awakened Mages, not hedge magicians (or exceptional citizens).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your general idea isn't wrong, but I think you missed some key points. I'll talk some math in a minute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486941#post1486941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True but it also doesn't really change the presentation either.<br /> <br /> None of the lore presented in Mage: The Ascension presents the Awakened as being an elite of the Traditions</div> </div> </div> </div>It does the first because it does the later, although as is common on all those games, the focus of the text on the player options makes it seems that those options are far more average than they actually are.<br /> <br /> Think about the fact that the average Attribute value for a human being is 2 and that 5 is world-class. The average mortal would be built with around 9 dots total to distribute among Attributes, equal chances for more or less (because it is a Normal Distribution). A hunter PC under the worse rules has 13 dots. A supernatural PC has 15. On Attributes alone we're talking about an extremely low percentage of the population even at the bare beginning. Each aspect of a PC is increasingly putting then at the very top.<br /> <br /> Our starting characters in WoD aren't even close to average people. They're over-the-top flukes that managed to become a part of their new over-the-top secret supernatural societies <i>and survive their beginnings</i>. Another characteristic of many splats, turnover is high. The challenges of the first nights for vampires, exposure to Paradox and dangerous phenomena for Mages, the sheer brutality of the War of Apocalypse for the Changing Breeds, people die <b><i>a lot</i></b>. You can meet 100 vampires in a city through the course of a year and yet it had no more than 30 at any given time, some left, a lot were Fledglings and died. Not necessarily standard, but can happen.<br /> <br /> We are talking supernatural societies whose bottom lines are already apex monsters compared to normal humans and a part of the hidden conspiracies controlling the world. The Neonate angry because the Elders have all the good things and they can't control more than a couple night clubs, a small gang and one officer at the precinct, from the POV of a mortal investigator is a secret shadow that ties those unrelated things, toying with unchecked power behind the scenes, and serving directly the masters of the world. And this mortal is actually right. Millionaires have trouble pretending to the level of power this Neonate have, and need to employ it far more judiciously. You're not the bottom of society, you're the bottom of the masters above even the elites.<br /> <br /> Consider now all those individual characters as some of the most powerful assets of their groups, not the bottom line, and review the numbers. The setting is not meant to have a representative of every small faction in every city with a million inhabitants, even if your chronicle may have it, because your chronicle is, by definition, special. A special moment in the lives of special people, your PCs. For many a Bloodline you don't need more than a dozen members around the world. You don't even need to have member of every Generation. A single immortal monster can be the sole representative of their culture for centuries before passing it down, because they're immortals. Mages and Werewolves have humans to carry on the bulk of their teachings and culture while they personally go out to be the legends those followers will sing about for generations.<br /> <br /> Are Generations exponential? I'm not sure. Most vampires Embrace slowly, a lot never do. Werewolves live a dangerous life where a lot of cubs don't make it alive through the Rites of Passage and many Cliath won't make it to their third year after Change. A single Mage isn't just a person that believes their Paradigm a lot, they're a <b><i>genius of their paradigm</i></b> that is transcending limitations and braving new possibilities since their awakening. And all of those have the resources and raw potential to cause such an astounding impact on the world that only their <i>few</i> equals can stop them from simply taking it all over.<br /> <br /> Sometimes sure, the games make things seem like they need more people than they give, maybe far more. <i>Maybe</i>. But I don't think the numbers are so lower than they should have for what they're really trying to represent. And the mortal &quot;companions&quot; aren't all that big of a problem, if every splat has 1 million &quot;human supporters&quot; and we consider VtM, WtA, MtA, WtO, CtD, MtR, HtR and DtF, that'l make 0,1% of the entire world's population. It is half the number of millionaires the world over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T11:24:06-07:00","id":1487029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486840#post1486840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the largest issues I feel with V5 is the fact that V5 feels like it wants to make everything Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which if true is funny in a bleak sort of way because Bloodlines was an attempt to approximate replicate Revised within the framework of a video game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T22:51:36-07:00","id":1492738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486672#post1486672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs do not believe that the Camarilla's Inner Circle, or the Sabbat's Regency are good methods for setting laws that apply to all members of their organizations, or setting policies to handle internal disputes, due to skewed priorities of such centralized power being threats to stable blood supply (as the Inner Circle and Regent are far removed from such concerns in any given city), and <b>want a system with greater authority given to local vampires in how large scale vampire society is run.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>But what does that really mean in practice? The Inner Circle is hardly micromanaging the affairs of individual cities. They local prince or council of primegon do whatever so long as the masquerade is kept and the anarchs/sabbat kept out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","user":"Alucard","date":". 09-10-2022, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T01:52:21-07:00","id":1492743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486884#post1486884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me of something I've noticed from movies: no matter how large or small the setting of a war movie is, it always seems to involve the same number of characters and even visible extras. Star Wars is a huge setting, with a huge chunk of the galaxy inhabited with hundreds of billions, perhaps trillions, of people and contributing soldiers. Movies like &quot;300&quot; and &quot;Troy&quot; are about tiny city-states fighting other tiny city-states. Yet somehow the visible number of main characters and extras are roughly the same. That's because these movies are about drama, and the number of characters in a war drama doesn't vary much regardless of the official populations involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to get into &quot;Great Man&quot; myths or anything but in some cases focusing on a few people even in larger scale settings makes a lot of sense. even outside of top-level politics, a few fields like, say, spy work or codebreaking can really be down to a few dozen people because it's not easy to replace people in these highly skilled contexts. (also SW does quite well in justifying why they're very skywalker focused, though most other recuring characters stretch things a little. There's the Force doing it all/It's fantasy and has no pretentions otherwise)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires are, at the top level, very difficult to replace. It makes some sense that we see a few big names quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T02:28:33-07:00","id":1492744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1492738#post1492738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what does that really mean in practice? The Inner Circle is hardly micromanaging the affairs of individual cities. They local prince or council of primegon do whatever do long as the masquerade is kept and the anarchs/sabbat kept out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means, in practice, the books aren't really well written to make a three way conflict between the Anarchs, Camarilla, and Sabbat engaging, and thus in any edition at least one of the Sects suffers because the writers don't work to give each a solid narrative space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T08:06:06-07:00","id":1492757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1486702#post1486702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Implosion of v5s core design group following the incident onyx path are the only surviving arm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on this for those of us, like me, who are not aware of the behind the scenes stuff?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-10T19:01:09-07:00","id":1492780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1492757#post1492757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on this for those of us, like me, who are not aware of the behind the scenes stuff?</div> </div> </div> </div><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>White Wolf publishes <i>Corebook</i>, August 2018</li> <li>Chicago by Night is kickstarted by OPP October 2018</li> <li><i>Anarch </i>and <i>Camarilla </i> November 2018</li> <li>Section in Camarilla is problematic and causes controversy November 2018</li> <li>Paradox <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20200709060229/https://www.white-wolf.com/post/a-message-from-white-wolf\" target=\"_blank\">reins in</a> White Wolf, disbanding the team and reforming it into the WoD team. &quot;White Wolf will develop the guiding principles for its vision of the World of Darkness, and give licensees the tools they need to create new, excellent products in this story world. White Wolf will no longer develop and publish these products internally.&quot; November 2018</li> <li>Chicago by Night releases February 2020</li> <li>Modiphius releases FoL, with glaring issues, March 2020</li> <li>Player's Guide is faced with delays (Rewrites due to Ravnos and Tzimisce being bad, Covid) 2019-2020</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/acclaimed-game-designer-justin-achilli-rejoins-world-of-darkness-as-brand-creative-lead\" target=\"_blank\">Achilli becomes creative lead </a>June 2020</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/media/press-releases/press-release/world-of-darkness-names-renegade-game-studios-publishing-partner-for-its-catalogue-of-tabletop-rpgs\" target=\"_blank\">Modiphius is replaced by Renegade,</a> the Player's Guide is temporarily replaced by the Companion, corebooks (like Werewolf) will now be developed in house, the rest by Renegade November 2020</li> </ol>That should be the major developmental changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T00:38:17-07:00","id":1492867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1492780#post1492780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>White Wolf publishes <i>Corebook</i>, August 2018</li> <li>Chicago by Night is kickstarted by OPP October 2018</li> <li><i>Anarch </i>and <i>Camarilla </i> November 2018</li> <li>Section in Camarilla is problematic and causes controversy November 2018</li> <li>Paradox <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://web.archive.org/web/20200709060229/https://www.white-wolf.com/post/a-message-from-white-wolf&amp;quot;]reins</a> in[/URL] White Wolf, disbanding the team and reforming it into the WoD team. &amp;quot;White Wolf will develop the guiding principles for its vision of the World of Darkness, and give licensees the tools they need to create new, excellent products in this story world. White Wolf will no longer develop and publish these products internally.&amp;quot; November 2018</li> <li>Chicago by Night releases February 2020</li> <li>Modiphius releases FoL, with glaring issues, March 2020</li> <li>Player's Guide is faced with delays (Rewrites due to Ravnos and Tzimisce being bad, Covid) 2019-2020</li> <li><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.worldofdarkness.com/news/acclaimed-game-designer-justin-achilli-rejoins-world-of-darkness-as-brand-creative-lead&amp;quot;]Achilli</a> becomes creative lead [/URL]June 2020</li> <li><a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/media/press-releases/press-release/world-of-darkness-names-renegade-game-studios-publishing-partner-for-its-catalogue-of-tabletop-rpgs&amp;quot;]Modiphius</a> is replaced by Renegade,[/URL] the Player's Guide is temporarily replaced by the Companion, corebooks (like Werewolf) will now be developed in house, the rest by Renegade November 2020</li> </ol>That should be the major developmental changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you dont me asking further, why were the Tzimisce &quot;bad&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Don't follow me, I'm lost too! But if you do...</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/gimmisky/</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.instagram.com/gimmisky/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11263-gimmisky","name":"Gimmisky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11263_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T05:15:13-07:00","id":1492879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gimmisky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486616-vampiric-nature-and-why-the-anarchs-will-always-fail-on-a-long-enough-timeline?p=1492867#post1492867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you dont me asking further, why were the Tzimisce &quot;bad&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that their write-up was bad and playtesters disliked it. I lack any primary sources and much information is under NDA so can't really give much certainty. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T10:10:37-07:00","id":1492894,"title":"","content":"That is strange we don't have any signature anarch characters at all. The Sabbat we have Vykos, Polina, Moncada and others. The Camarilla had Hardstadt, Theo Bell, Jan Pieztrizoon, Helen, and Kevin Jackson. The Independants had Fatima, Lucida, Sigfried, Mithras, Hesha and Lazarus. But when it comes to the Anarchs there really isn't any stand out ones.<br /> <br /> I don't see my character wanting having anything to do with Starek or the defector Bell at all. Though with the Ventrue character any interaction would be him stacking her in the heart and leaving her out somewhere to greet the sun out of a sense of lingering ethics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:13:13-07:00","id":1492918,"title":"","content":"Um, there's a bunch of them? The problem was that the biggest period in the oWoD run for signature characters was after the shift towards downplaying the Anarchs for the biggest Sect war. With the Anarchs out of focus (even with plenty of name Anarchs in the books that are major players in various events) they didn't make book covers or get action figures. The biggest publicity boost was Bloodlines, as it revitalized Smiling Jack as the archetypal old Anarch, and introduced Damsel as the icon for modern bomb throwing Anarchs (and Damsel remains quite popular), and Jeanette Voreman. Characters like Tyler or Lugoj are there, just not featured as much as they could be; and the books frequently have the oldest and most powerful Anarchs flop around a lot between allegiances after awhile. There's also Jeremy McNeil, Christopher Houghton, Salvador Garcia, and son on.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of big name NPCs in the Anarchs. They're just not as prominently focused on in a lot of the fiction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}